1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,000
Subs by Mkrm

2
00:01:26,460 --> 00:01:28,530
Coach Tony.

3
00:01:28,540 --> 00:01:29,340
You definitely think

4
00:01:30,080 --> 00:01:31,230
it was me who stole the food,

5
00:01:31,240 --> 00:01:31,710
I'm not here to sell anything.

6
00:01:32,200 --> 00:01:33,660
I'm here to discuss a Sponsorship.

7
00:01:34,120 --> 00:01:35,100
Your hair is so unique.

8
00:01:35,560 --> 00:01:36,540
You could shoot a wig commercial.

9
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:37,500
What?

10
00:01:37,660 --> 00:01:39,390
If your company Sponsors our Team,

11
00:01:39,400 --> 00:01:40,350
it would be

12
00:01:40,360 --> 00:01:42,300
a huge promotional boost for you guys.

13
00:01:43,240 --> 00:01:44,220
If he were really that good,

14
00:01:45,160 --> 00:01:47,100
he would've reacted to me provoking him so obviously.

15
00:01:51,400 --> 00:01:52,380
What a dump.

16
00:01:52,840 --> 00:01:55,740
It was so hard to find.

17
00:01:56,000 --> 00:01:59,500
Episode 8

18
00:02:04,840 --> 00:02:07,260
Ouch... ouch...

19
00:02:10,600 --> 00:02:12,540
Ouch, ouch. It hurts so much!

20
00:02:14,440 --> 00:02:15,900
It's all that stupid Director's fault.

21
00:02:16,360 --> 00:02:19,260
Just 1 line of dialogue, and he
made me shoot it over 20 times.

22
00:02:19,720 --> 00:02:23,580
Making me walk back and forth over and over again! Ouch!

23
00:02:24,520 --> 00:02:28,380
Hey! Driver! Hey, driver!

24
00:02:29,600 --> 00:02:31,000
Wait! Wait!

25
00:02:32,200 --> 00:02:34,140
Miss, are you an Actress?

26
00:02:34,600 --> 00:02:36,060
How did you know?

27
00:02:37,380 --> 00:02:40,380
Isn't it obvious? Never mind looking at people,

28
00:02:40,540 --> 00:02:41,820
even when I'm picking out a chicken at the market,

29
00:02:42,760 --> 00:02:44,220
I can tell which one's good and which one isn't

30
00:02:45,160 --> 00:02:46,620
with just one glance.

31
00:02:48,040 --> 00:02:49,980
That outfit, and your whole vibe...

32
00:02:50,440 --> 00:02:51,420
You look just like a celebrity.

33
00:02:51,880 --> 00:02:53,340
I just finished filming a TV drama.

34
00:02:54,280 --> 00:02:55,740
I came by on my way to visit my Daughter.

35
00:02:56,200 --> 00:02:58,140
Really? You're a TV actress?

36
00:03:03,880 --> 00:03:05,340
Us too! Let's get in on this!

37
00:03:06,280 --> 00:03:07,260
My turn!

38
00:03:07,720 --> 00:03:10,140
Ready... 1, 2, 3!

39
00:03:11,560 --> 00:03:12,540
Can I have your autograph?

40
00:03:13,000 --> 00:03:13,950
Your movies are great! Can you sign for me?

41
00:03:14,320 --> 00:03:23,580
1,2,3,4!

42
00:03:28,840 --> 00:03:30,300
Sir, I can't read this signature at all.

43
00:03:31,240 --> 00:03:33,660
That's just how celebrity signatures are.

44
00:03:39,400 --> 00:03:40,860
Excuse me, what's going on over there?

45
00:03:41,320 --> 00:03:42,300
I heard there's a Celebrity over there.

46
00:03:42,760 --> 00:03:44,700
We're all trying to get her autograph.

47
00:03:45,160 --> 00:03:46,590
A Celebrity?

48
00:03:46,600 --> 00:03:47,860
Then we should go check it out, too.

49
00:03:48,120 --> 00:03:49,470
Get back here!

50
00:03:49,480 --> 00:03:50,460
What's there to see?

51
00:03:50,920 --> 00:03:53,210
Based on the years of experience my Mom passed down to me,

52
00:03:53,220 --> 00:03:53,820
I can easily tell,

53
00:03:54,560 --> 00:03:55,710
that only background extras

54
00:03:55,720 --> 00:03:58,110
would come to a place like this to give autographs.

55
00:03:58,120 --> 00:04:00,540
Me first! Sign for me! It's my turn! My turn!

56
00:04:01,180 --> 00:04:02,460
Monica.

57
00:04:04,540 --> 00:04:06,780
Monica! It's Mom! Mom's right here!

58
00:04:09,640 --> 00:04:10,620
Monica.

59
00:04:18,280 --> 00:04:20,220
Let Mom take a look at you! Let me see!

60
00:04:20,680 --> 00:04:23,100
Why are you so dark?

61
00:04:23,560 --> 00:04:24,540
Did you not listen to what Mom told you?

62
00:04:24,600 --> 00:04:25,980
You forgot to put on sunscreen!

63
00:04:26,000 --> 00:04:27,000
I'm fine

64
00:04:28,360 --> 00:04:30,780
Look at you, all dark and skinny.

65
00:04:31,720 --> 00:04:33,180
What? Haven't you been eating well here?

66
00:04:33,640 --> 00:04:34,620
No, it's not that, Mom.

67
00:04:36,520 --> 00:04:37,500
I just don't get it.

68
00:04:37,960 --> 00:04:39,420
Why does your School have to send you

69
00:04:39,880 --> 00:04:42,780
to a place like this to train? It's way too harsh!

70
00:04:43,240 --> 00:04:45,180
Mom brought you a ton of good food this time.

71
00:04:45,440 --> 00:04:46,140
Look.

72
00:04:47,560 --> 00:04:49,020
Let's take it out once we get back to the dorm.

73
00:04:50,920 --> 00:04:53,820
Sweetie, how did you get dark circles under your eyes?

74
00:04:54,560 --> 00:04:56,700
What's wrong? Didn't you sleep well at night?

75
00:04:57,440 --> 00:04:58,620
It's because of listening to music.

76
00:04:59,560 --> 00:05:00,540
Listening to music?

77
00:05:01,960 --> 00:05:04,860
How can there be music in the dorms at night?

78
00:05:05,320 --> 00:05:07,740
It's... it's because Mini brought it.

79
00:05:08,200 --> 00:05:10,140
Mini? Which one is Mini?

80
00:05:11,560 --> 00:05:12,540
What music?

81
00:05:13,960 --> 00:05:15,390
You're Mini?

82
00:05:15,400 --> 00:05:16,380
Hello, ma'am.

83
00:05:16,840 --> 00:05:18,780
I'm Monica's roommate, Mini.

84
00:05:20,680 --> 00:05:22,620
Mini, I don't mean to scold you,

85
00:05:23,360 --> 00:05:25,020
but when everyone else is trying to sleep at night,

86
00:05:25,180 --> 00:05:26,910
how can you be listening to music?

87
00:05:26,920 --> 00:05:28,380
Monica, that's not true!

88
00:05:28,640 --> 00:05:30,780
My Sister was out practicing Yo-Yo last night

89
00:05:31,040 --> 00:05:32,220
and didn't get back until really late.

90
00:05:32,480 --> 00:05:33,220
Leo and I can both vouch for that.

91
00:05:35,560 --> 00:05:36,060
It's not like that, Mom.

92
00:05:36,520 --> 00:05:38,460
I was the one who took Mini's MP3 player

93
00:05:38,720 --> 00:05:39,420
to listen to music.

94
00:05:41,320 --> 00:05:42,780
Well, I wasn't entirely wrong, then.

95
00:05:43,240 --> 00:05:47,100
You two share a dorm room.
You should be looking out for each other.

96
00:05:47,560 --> 00:05:50,430
When she comes back late,
it disturbs other people's rest, too.

97
00:05:50,440 --> 00:05:51,420
I actually think Monica

98
00:05:51,680 --> 00:05:53,310
should be thanking Mini.

99
00:05:53,320 --> 00:05:54,780
She was the one who borrowed Mini's MP3 player first.

100
00:05:55,720 --> 00:05:57,180
And as for what time Mini comes back,

101
00:05:58,120 --> 00:05:59,580
it shouldn't have any effect on someone

102
00:06:00,040 --> 00:06:01,020
who's staying up all night listening to music anyway.

103
00:06:01,480 --> 00:06:01,950
Yeah, exactly!

104
00:06:27,400 --> 00:06:30,780
For the next couple of days, just come stay with Mom, okay?

105
00:06:31,720 --> 00:06:33,180
That way, that immature Mini

106
00:06:34,120 --> 00:06:35,580
won't disturb your sleep anymore.

107
00:06:37,480 --> 00:06:40,380
Just trust Mom's judgment on this.

108
00:06:43,240 --> 00:06:45,180
Look, I brought you some bug spray.

109
00:06:45,640 --> 00:06:46,620
Mom thinks of everything, doesn't she?

110
00:06:48,520 --> 00:06:50,460
You kids... what kind of ridiculous training is this?

111
00:06:51,400 --> 00:06:52,860
It's ruining your skin.

112
00:06:53,320 --> 00:06:55,260
The most important thing in life is a woman's skin.

113
00:06:55,720 --> 00:06:56,700
Ugh, I know!

114
00:06:57,640 --> 00:07:01,020
And look at you. You even forgot to bring conditioner.

115
00:07:01,480 --> 00:07:03,900
Taking care of your hair is just as important, young lady.

116
00:07:04,840 --> 00:07:05,820
And, calcium pills.

117
00:07:06,760 --> 00:07:09,660
The hardest thing for me to accept is that you
always forget to take your pills!

118
00:07:10,120 --> 00:07:11,580
How many times has Mom told you?

119
00:07:12,040 --> 00:07:13,500
While your body is still growing

120
00:07:13,560 --> 00:07:14,940
if you don't keep up with your calcium intake

121
00:07:15,400 --> 00:07:17,820
the consequences will be unimaginable!

122
00:07:18,280 --> 00:07:19,260
As a woman,

123
00:07:19,720 --> 00:07:21,660
your figure is the most important thing of all.

124
00:07:21,820 --> 00:07:23,100
But last time you said

125
00:07:23,560 --> 00:07:25,020
that artistic temperament was the most important.

126
00:07:25,960 --> 00:07:27,900
Well, artistic temperament is important, too, of course.

127
00:07:28,160 --> 00:07:29,140
Then what actually is the most important thing?

128
00:07:30,000 --> 00:07:30,900
Skin, hair, figure,

129
00:07:31,040 --> 00:07:32,700
and artistic temperament are all important.

130
00:07:34,120 --> 00:07:37,500
Back in my day, when I had all those things,

131
00:07:37,960 --> 00:07:40,380
opportunities were as plentiful as ants on the ground.

132
00:07:40,440 --> 00:07:41,820
Alright, Mom, enough.

133
00:07:42,080 --> 00:07:43,740
And now all you can do is land extra roles in Mhows.

134
00:07:44,200 --> 00:07:48,030
You brat! How can you talk to your mother like that?

135
00:07:48,040 --> 00:07:50,460
If I hadn't been so busy raising you,
I would have maintained my looks!

136
00:07:50,920 --> 00:07:52,860
You ungrateful child.

137
00:08:01,660 --> 00:08:03,420
"Baby's Cradle"

138
00:08:08,400 --> 00:08:09,500
Wait, wait, wait!

139
00:08:10,600 --> 00:08:12,060
Sorry! Sorry, just pause for a second!

140
00:08:15,400 --> 00:08:19,740
You must be burning up, sweetie.

141
00:08:20,200 --> 00:08:21,180
Here, let Mom fan you.

142
00:08:21,640 --> 00:08:22,620
Sorry, everyone! So sorry!

143
00:08:23,740 --> 00:08:25,020
You guys keep going. Keep going.

144
00:08:31,800 --> 00:08:34,140
Next up, "Around the World."

145
00:08:36,500 --> 00:08:37,500
Wait! Wait!

146
00:08:37,960 --> 00:08:39,900
Sorry! Sorry!

147
00:08:41,320 --> 00:08:43,740
Monica, here, have some water.

148
00:08:47,560 --> 00:08:48,060
I'm dying of heat!

149
00:08:49,480 --> 00:08:50,430
Hurry up! Come on!

150
00:08:50,440 --> 00:08:51,390
Sorry! I'm sorry!

151
00:08:51,400 --> 00:08:52,860
Keep going! Keep going!

152
00:08:56,860 --> 00:08:58,620
Next, "Around the World."

153
00:08:59,500 --> 00:09:02,000
1,2,3,4

154
00:09:03,000 --> 00:09:04,000
Wait, wait!

155
00:09:07,720 --> 00:09:10,590
I have a little suggestion about that move you just did.

156
00:09:10,600 --> 00:09:12,060
"Around the World."

157
00:09:18,280 --> 00:09:19,740
Baby's Cradle.

158
00:09:24,520 --> 00:09:26,940
"Eiffel Tower."

159
00:09:32,200 --> 00:09:33,660
"Stone Pass."

160
00:09:38,440 --> 00:09:39,900
It's "Forward Pass."

161
00:09:41,800 --> 00:09:43,740
What's the difference between a
"Stone Pass" and a "Forward Pass" anyway?

162
00:09:44,380 --> 00:09:45,660
You're just memorizing by names.

163
00:09:46,780 --> 00:09:48,060
Alright, alright, keep going!

164
00:09:58,600 --> 00:10:01,500
Mom, skipping Training makes me feel uneasy.

165
00:10:02,440 --> 00:10:04,390
What's there to feel uneasy about
with your Mom right here beside you?

166
00:10:06,080 --> 00:10:07,260
Listen to me.

167
00:10:08,000 --> 00:10:09,660
Training with that kind of high intensity

168
00:10:10,120 --> 00:10:11,580
will age you really fast.

169
00:10:12,040 --> 00:10:13,500
You have to learn to take care of yourself.

170
00:10:14,440 --> 00:10:16,860
But I should at least ask the Captain
for permission to skip practice.

171
00:10:17,800 --> 00:10:20,700
Don't you worry about that. Mom already thought of that.

172
00:10:27,880 --> 00:10:31,260
Don't panic. Stay still. Mom's right here.

173
00:10:35,160 --> 00:10:36,510
Who is it?

174
00:10:36,520 --> 00:10:37,980
Ma'am, it's Mark.

175
00:10:38,720 --> 00:10:39,900
Is Monica in?

176
00:10:40,200 --> 00:10:41,900
Hold on a second.

177
00:10:43,720 --> 00:10:44,700
Ma'am.

178
00:10:46,600 --> 00:10:48,060
Please keep your voice down.

179
00:10:48,520 --> 00:10:49,980
Monica isn't feeling well. She's resting.

180
00:10:51,880 --> 00:10:52,860
What's wrong?

181
00:10:53,800 --> 00:10:57,180
She has a bit of a fever...
no, wait, more of an upset stomach.

182
00:10:58,120 --> 00:11:00,060
Looks like she'll need a couple days to recover.

183
00:11:00,520 --> 00:11:01,500
Does she need to see a Doctor?

184
00:11:01,960 --> 00:11:04,380
No, no. I'm her mother, I know best.

185
00:11:04,840 --> 00:11:06,300
She's just worn out from Training.

186
00:11:07,040 --> 00:11:07,940
You just focus on your practice.

187
00:11:08,200 --> 00:11:09,660
I'll send her back when she's feeling better.

188
00:11:10,600 --> 00:11:13,020
But... we're learning new drills today.

189
00:11:13,480 --> 00:11:14,940
If she falls behind

190
00:11:15,400 --> 00:11:16,380
I'm afraid she won't be able to catch up.

191
00:11:17,320 --> 00:11:19,740
She's sick, what can we do about it?

192
00:11:20,760 --> 00:11:23,580
Alright then. I'll head out. Take good care of her.

193
00:11:24,220 --> 00:11:25,500
Okay, goodbye.

194
00:11:29,320 --> 00:11:30,780
Mark! Mark!

195
00:11:33,440 --> 00:11:35,580
Here. I stayed up late last night and

196
00:11:35,740 --> 00:11:36,940
put a lot of thought into these notes.

197
00:11:37,000 --> 00:11:38,460
Please pass them along to the Coach for me.

198
00:11:38,920 --> 00:11:40,830
And have the Coach forward them
to the School Administration.

199
00:11:40,840 --> 00:11:43,740
I need the School Leaders to give
this some very serious consideration.

200
00:11:45,340 --> 00:11:46,620
Right...

201
00:11:47,080 --> 00:11:48,540
Alright, alright, bye!

202
00:11:48,800 --> 00:11:50,000
- Wait...

203
00:11:58,600 --> 00:12:00,930
Go on, eat up. Mom will peel another one for you.

204
00:12:05,800 --> 00:12:06,780
Who is it?

205
00:12:20,280 --> 00:12:21,660
Can I help you?

206
00:12:22,400 --> 00:12:25,020
Ma'am, I was hoping I could see Monica.

207
00:12:25,960 --> 00:12:27,250
She's doing much better, thank you.

208
00:12:28,840 --> 00:12:31,260
Ma'am, could I maybe get your autograph?

209
00:12:32,860 --> 00:12:34,140
Well, come on in.

210
00:12:38,440 --> 00:12:39,420
Have a seat, sit down.

211
00:12:41,320 --> 00:12:43,740
Monica is so lucky to have a Mom like you.

212
00:12:44,200 --> 00:12:45,660
Here, have an apple. It's washed.

213
00:12:48,040 --> 00:12:50,940
Oh, and ma'am, could you sign right here?

214
00:12:51,400 --> 00:12:52,380
Right here.

215
00:12:58,400 --> 00:12:59,100
Take your time eating.

216
00:13:04,540 --> 00:13:05,820
Who are you?

217
00:13:06,280 --> 00:13:08,220
Ma'am, I'm Matthew.

218
00:13:09,160 --> 00:13:10,620
What does he want?

219
00:13:19,720 --> 00:13:20,700
Ma'am, have some water.

220
00:13:22,600 --> 00:13:25,500
Ma'am, the staff in the dining hall
talk about you all the time.

221
00:13:25,960 --> 00:13:27,420
They say not only are you so kind and friendly,

222
00:13:27,880 --> 00:13:30,780
but you don't have any of that Celebrity
arrogance about you. Isn't that right?

223
00:13:31,240 --> 00:13:35,100
Oh, please, please. They're just flattering me.

224
00:13:36,040 --> 00:13:38,430
They also say you and Monica don't
look like Mother and Daughter.

225
00:13:38,440 --> 00:13:39,900
They say you look more like her older sister.

226
00:13:41,800 --> 00:13:43,260
Ma'am, you know what?

227
00:13:43,520 --> 00:13:45,180
Monica is the prettiest girl in our whole School.

228
00:13:45,640 --> 00:13:46,620
Prettiest in her Class, too.

229
00:13:47,080 --> 00:13:48,060
Prettiest on the Team.

230
00:13:48,520 --> 00:13:49,980
And the prettiest girl at this whole Training Base.

231
00:13:50,440 --> 00:13:51,420
Right, Matthew?

232
00:13:51,880 --> 00:13:53,820
Oh, for sure.
She definitely got her looks from you, ma'am.

233
00:13:55,240 --> 00:13:56,700
Eat up, eat up.

234
00:13:59,560 --> 00:14:01,880
Ma'am, you guys won't ever need to leave the room.

235
00:14:02,620 --> 00:14:04,380
Whatever you need to eat, just let us know.

236
00:14:04,840 --> 00:14:05,790
We'll bring it right to you.

237
00:14:05,800 --> 00:14:07,260
Yeah, we'll deliver it for you!

238
00:14:22,600 --> 00:14:25,500
Monica! What made you come back all of a sudden?

239
00:14:25,960 --> 00:14:27,870
What do you mean, "all of a sudden"?

240
00:14:27,880 --> 00:14:28,860
I've been staying here the whole time.

241
00:14:29,600 --> 00:14:30,500
No, that's not what I meant.

242
00:14:30,760 --> 00:14:33,180
Weren't you staying at your Mom's
place the past couple of days?

243
00:14:33,640 --> 00:14:34,140
I thought

244
00:14:34,600 --> 00:14:36,540
you wouldn't come back until after your Mom left.

245
00:14:37,000 --> 00:14:38,430
You obviously didn't want me to come back.

246
00:14:38,440 --> 00:14:39,900
Me being back makes things
Inconvenient for you, doesn't it?

247
00:14:41,320 --> 00:14:42,780
What do you mean "inconvenient"?

248
00:14:44,200 --> 00:14:46,140
Stop pretending you don't know what I mean.

249
00:14:46,300 --> 00:14:47,100
There's no need for that.

250
00:14:51,200 --> 00:14:52,380
Monica.

251
00:14:54,280 --> 00:14:56,700
I honestly have no idea what you're talking about.

252
00:14:57,160 --> 00:15:00,060
Stop pretending. You're always acting so naive and innocent.

253
00:15:00,520 --> 00:15:02,460
Maybe that works on guys like Leo and Mark,

254
00:15:02,920 --> 00:15:03,900
but I'm not falling for it anymore.

255
00:15:05,320 --> 00:15:06,300
How can you talk like that?

256
00:15:07,240 --> 00:15:09,180
When have I ever tried to fool them?

257
00:15:09,640 --> 00:15:11,580
And when have I ever tried to fool you?

258
00:15:12,040 --> 00:15:13,500
You've never fooled me?

259
00:15:13,960 --> 00:15:15,900
You know perfectly well that I met Leo first.

260
00:15:16,360 --> 00:15:17,820
I shared all my feelings about it with you.

261
00:15:18,260 --> 00:15:19,740
But you...

262
00:15:23,080 --> 00:15:25,020
You went behind my back to cozy up to Leo.

263
00:15:25,280 --> 00:15:26,940
You even started secretly practicing with him.

264
00:15:27,400 --> 00:15:28,830
And I was left completely in the dark.

265
00:15:28,840 --> 00:15:30,300
Do you call that fair Competition?

266
00:15:31,420 --> 00:15:34,620
I didn't... I didn't do anything behind your back!

267
00:15:35,080 --> 00:15:37,020
Leo practiced with us

268
00:15:37,960 --> 00:15:38,910
because of Mickey!

269
00:15:38,920 --> 00:15:39,900
Save your excuses.

270
00:15:40,840 --> 00:15:42,040
Honestly, I saw right through you a long time ago.

271
00:15:43,040 --> 00:15:45,180
When I first introduced you to Leo
during my beautiful encounter moment,

272
00:15:45,640 --> 00:15:47,780
I could already tell look in your eyes completely changed!

273
00:15:48,040 --> 00:15:50,460
I just didn't expect you to go this far.

274
00:15:51,400 --> 00:15:52,380
What did I do?

275
00:15:53,600 --> 00:15:56,220
I really don't know what you're talking about.

276
00:15:57,160 --> 00:15:58,620
You honestly think I don't know?

277
00:15:59,080 --> 00:16:00,060
You're playing games.

278
00:16:01,480 --> 00:16:04,860
What do you mean, "playing games"? This is ridiculous.

279
00:16:06,760 --> 00:16:08,220
If you weren't playing games,

280
00:16:08,420 --> 00:16:10,620
why did Mark constantly defend you back then?

281
00:16:11,080 --> 00:16:12,540
And now that you're on the Team,

282
00:16:12,700 --> 00:16:14,460
you're pulling the same tricks on Leo.

283
00:16:16,840 --> 00:16:18,300
Your tactics are so subtle.

284
00:16:18,760 --> 00:16:21,660
Too bad I can see right through them.

285
00:16:22,600 --> 00:16:24,060
Monica, I get it now.

286
00:16:25,280 --> 00:16:26,910
If you're upset because...

287
00:16:26,920 --> 00:16:28,860
Leo spoke up for me that day,

288
00:16:29,800 --> 00:16:32,220
I can understand that. But

289
00:16:32,680 --> 00:16:34,140
for you to say I'm playing games

290
00:16:35,080 --> 00:16:37,020
is something I really can't understand.

291
00:16:37,560 --> 00:16:38,460
I'm not angry

292
00:16:38,920 --> 00:16:39,710
just because Leo spoke up for you!

293
00:16:40,640 --> 00:16:41,340
He's nothing.

294
00:16:41,800 --> 00:16:44,220
Just a little Runner-Up who's
too scared to even make a move.

295
00:16:44,680 --> 00:16:46,620
What really makes me mad is you playing dumb,

296
00:16:46,980 --> 00:16:49,980
acting weak, acting pitiful,
just to get sympathy from boys.

297
00:16:50,440 --> 00:16:51,420
That's your tactic.

298
00:16:51,880 --> 00:16:53,820
And to me, it just comes off as totally fake.

299
00:16:54,000 --> 00:16:55,260
Do you get it now?

300
00:16:55,720 --> 00:16:59,580
But that's... that's just a difference in our personalities!

301
00:17:00,520 --> 00:17:02,910
Well then, couldn't I just as easily say

302
00:17:02,920 --> 00:17:06,780
that you're the one acting noble, acting bubbly,
acting trendy, acting like a celebrity?

303
00:17:08,000 --> 00:17:10,140
Wouldn't those count as tactics, too?

304
00:17:11,080 --> 00:17:12,540
Of course those aren't tactics.

305
00:17:12,600 --> 00:17:13,980
Besides, it's not like I used any of that

306
00:17:14,140 --> 00:17:15,420
to get onto this Team.

307
00:17:15,880 --> 00:17:17,820
Well, I didn't use anything to get on the Team, either.

308
00:17:18,280 --> 00:17:19,740
Oh, really?

309
00:17:20,000 --> 00:17:21,630
If you truly believe you got on this Team
based on your own Skill,

310
00:17:21,640 --> 00:17:23,580
then let's have a Match right now and settle it.

311
00:17:24,040 --> 00:17:25,980
We'll just see who's better.

312
00:17:27,400 --> 00:17:30,270
Monica, if you think being good at Yo-Yo

313
00:17:30,280 --> 00:17:33,660
gives you the right to talk to people like this,
then I accept your challenge.

314
00:17:34,780 --> 00:17:37,020
But if I beat you,

315
00:17:37,660 --> 00:17:39,630
you have to stop with these pointless attacks.

316
00:17:41,280 --> 00:17:42,780
You think you can beat me?

317
00:17:47,080 --> 00:17:49,020
I'll be the Referee for you two!

318
00:17:49,480 --> 00:17:50,430
No way. That's not fair.

319
00:17:51,880 --> 00:17:52,860
Then what do you suggest?

320
00:17:54,000 --> 00:17:55,710
We'll do it together.

321
00:17:55,720 --> 00:17:57,660
Fine. Ready...

322
00:17:58,120 --> 00:18:01,020
Go!

323
00:18:34,000 --> 00:18:38,500
[Name: Mini | Team: Jianghai]
[Yo-Yo: Phantom Light Wheel | Special Move: Phantom Flying Wheel]

324
00:18:40,000 --> 00:18:43,500
[Name: Monica | Team: Jianghai]
[Yo-Yo: Super Lightspeed | Special Move: Super Power Lightspeed]

325
00:18:50,440 --> 00:18:51,900
Go, Monica!

326
00:18:57,160 --> 00:18:58,140
That was beautiful!

327
00:19:29,800 --> 00:19:31,260
Go, Monica!

328
00:19:44,680 --> 00:19:46,140
She lost, she lost!

329
00:19:48,040 --> 00:19:49,500
Why'd you turn on the fan?!

330
00:19:49,960 --> 00:19:52,380
It's hot! Can't I turn on the fan?

331
00:19:53,320 --> 00:19:54,300
Don't you realize

332
00:19:54,760 --> 00:19:57,180
how much the wind can mess with a Yo-Yo?

333
00:19:57,640 --> 00:19:58,620
How was I supposed to know?

334
00:19:59,560 --> 00:20:01,020
You did that on purpose to sabotage her! It doesn't count!

335
00:20:01,960 --> 00:20:03,900
You kid, how can you say that?

336
00:20:04,360 --> 00:20:06,300
A loss is a loss. You can't just say it doesn't count.

337
00:20:07,240 --> 00:20:09,660
It's so hot out, turning on a fan is perfectly normal.

338
00:20:09,820 --> 00:20:11,100
Mom.

339
00:20:14,440 --> 00:20:14,940
Mickey.

340
00:20:52,840 --> 00:20:55,260
You lost one little match and now you're all upset?

341
00:20:56,480 --> 00:20:57,660
No, I'm not.

342
00:21:00,040 --> 00:21:01,020
Mickey told me all about it.

343
00:21:01,960 --> 00:21:04,380
A match like that isn't worth getting worked up over.

344
00:21:05,800 --> 00:21:09,660
I know my Yo-Yo skills aren't that great.

345
00:21:10,120 --> 00:21:11,580
But...

346
00:21:12,520 --> 00:21:13,980
It feels like I just can't break
through to the next level.

347
00:21:16,840 --> 00:21:18,780
Don't be so impatient. Just take it one step at a time.

348
00:21:20,200 --> 00:21:23,100
So... can you help me get better?

